# CHANGELOG is append-only and every change adds an entry at the SAME anchor (the top of
# `## [Unreleased]`), so two parallel agents conflict on it essentially every time. `union`
# tells git to keep BOTH sides of a conflicting hunk instead of stopping, which is exactly
# the right semantics here and removes a hand-resolution step from every parallel merge.
# Tradeoff, accepted knowingly: it never conflicts, so two genuinely overlapping entries can
# interleave or duplicate. That surfaces at review, where it is cheap, instead of at merge,
# where it blocks.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
